<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Brain-Training on BMStudyHub</title><link>https://www.bmstudyhub.top/tags/brain-training/</link><description>Recent content in Brain-Training on BMStudyHub</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 01 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.bmstudyhub.top/tags/brain-training/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Dual N-Back Training Game</title><link>https://www.bmstudyhub.top/games/nback/</link><pubDate>Mon, 20 May 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.bmstudyhub.top/games/nback/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="how-to-play"&gt;How to Play&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dual N-Back asks you to compare the &lt;strong&gt;current round&lt;/strong&gt; with the round that appeared &lt;strong&gt;N steps earlier&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For example, in &lt;strong&gt;2-back&lt;/strong&gt;, compare the current round with the one from two rounds ago:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Round&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Position&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Letter&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;What to compare&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Top left&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;C&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Build history&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Center&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;F&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Build history&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Top left&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;B&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Compare with round 1: position matches&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Bottom right&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;F&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Compare with round 2: letter matches&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each round has two things to track:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>